    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d580">

                <pb facs="0967" n="897" xml:id="pg897"/>

                <head>No. 581.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Davis to Mr. Baker.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi><lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-01-18"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 18,
                        1883</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 199.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Adverting to previous correspondence upon
                    the subject, I have now to inclose for your information copy of a note from the
                    British minister here, of the 15th instant, concerning the custody of ships’
                    papers when in the ports of Venezuela.<anchor n="*" xml:id="d580-f1"/></p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN DAVIS,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d580-f1" n="*" xml:id="d580-f1-content">
                <p>For inclosure see document No. 280, <ref target="#pg491">page 491</ref>.</p>
